# Legacy SFA app — read-only reference

The old **SFA** app (Next.js 14, being retired) is available inside this repo at
`./SFA` — a **symlink** to the sibling `../SFA` checkout, so you can read and
search it without leaving the AIOS-SFA workspace. It is **gitignored** (see
`.gitignore` → "Local project folders") and never committed here.

## Rules
- **Read-only.** Never edit, create, or delete files under `./SFA`. Build all new
  work in `packages/*`. If `./SFA` is missing, recreate the link with
  `ln -s ../SFA SFA` from the repo root.
- **Port, don't reimplement.** Translate legacy business logic into typed NestJS
  services + Mongoose schemas. Preserve `legacySmartSuiteId` on any schema that
  maps to legacy data.

## Where to look in `./SFA`
- `SFA/app/api/**` — ~69 legacy API routes (behaviour source-of-truth).
- `SFA/lib/**` — data-access + domain logic. Key ports:
  - `SFA/lib/performance/getPerformanceBuckets.ts` — scorecard math.
  - `SFA/lib/leadSources.ts` — 14 canonical lead sources.
  - `SFA/lib/roles.ts` — legacy Clerk role → new permission mapping.
  - `SFA/lib/smartsuite.ts`, `SFA/lib/intake/` — SmartSuite access + intake.

## Legacy data model
The SmartSuite tables (the migration source-of-record model) are documented in
`docs/smartsuite-tables/`. Use these when modeling Mongo collections.
